30,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Transport costs vary wildly depending on distance. Public beds seem cheap, but we must be careful with the total budget.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Public bookings are an administrative nightmare. However, avoiding on-site cooking duties would save the organizers significant time.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It seems shared living is the only way to get year-groups to actually bond. Also, some members stop coming if it's too far.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Our own hall is overcrowded during vacation. Meanwhile, some inland facilities have very strict, cramped sleeping arrangements.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Fixed-headcount lets are risky because the group pays for late cancellations. Also, many members can't commute daily without overnight stays.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, if fixed lets are risky, we should avoid private inns. @Toshio, is the public booking process really that bad?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Yes, one mistake in the application requires a full restart. It's a huge time sink for the organizers.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minako,,"If we stay on campus, we lose the shared living aspect that the seniors emphasized for bonding.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Minako. But if the inland dorms are too crowded, the training quality will suffer due to lack of sleep.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the transport costs you mentioned suggest that staying local is the only way to keep the fee low and fair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Staying local is safest for the budget, but we must account for those who need beds.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we avoid the public lottery and the cooking duties, we save the organizers' sanity.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We need a balance. If we don't prioritize the social environment, the club will continue to fragment.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We need a place where people can actually rest. Cramped dorms or split schedules are not ideal.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We must avoid any arrangement where the remaining members subsidize those who drop out.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"It seems we are torn between cost, effort, and quality. Let's see the options.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Asuka,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
