55,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is the most budget-stable. Option A's distance and Option C's rates are less predictable.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A removes cooking duties, but Option C's lottery is a nightmare. Option B is easiest to organize.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option A and C offer shared living. Option B fails to address the year-group divide.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C sounds like the cramped dorms I read about. Option B's schedule is too fragmented. Option A is best for rest.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is a financial risk due to the non-refundable deposit. Option B is unfair to those commuting.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, Option B still requires paying for beds for some. But Option A's transport cost would be huge.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, is the social aspect worth the risk of the organizers burning out on a public booking for Option C?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Yes, because the club is falling apart. But Option A also provides shared living without the lottery.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Option A provides a whole building. That means better sleep and better bonding than Option B or C.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I still worry about the deposit for Option A. However, Option C's public system is also rigid.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we choose A, we must be very strict about the headcount to avoid the deficit I fear.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is better than C for the organizers. B is the easiest, but maybe too boring.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minako,,Option A satisfies the need for shared living and avoids the public booking mess.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for A. It's the only one that guarantees decent sleep and a cohesive environment.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we can manage the deposit risk, A is better than B for those who can't commute.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'll concede to A if we set a strict payment deadline to cover the deposit.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I'm in for A. No cooking, no lottery.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Minako,,A is the best for the club's future.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,A is my choice.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for A as well.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
